T","DK","DKL","KNTK","LBRT","NOG","OII","PTEN","TNK","TRMD"],"beta":1.15,"beta_5y":1.15,"kd":4.5,"tax":21,"growth_10y":[5.4,4.9,4.4,4,3.8,3.5,3.2,2.9,2.6,2.2],"g1":5.4,"g2":3.5,"g":2.25,"wacc":9.17,"ev":5267.5,"fmp_official_ev":5267.5,"enterpriseValueBasis":"USD market capitalization + USD debt - USD cash and short-term investments","dcf_model_ev":7403.4,"ev_to_ebitda":3.4,"debt_to_ebitda":0.46,"net_debt_to_ebitda":0.16,"f_score":8,"f_score_breakdown":[{"id":1,"category":"盈利能力","desc":"資產回報率 ROA > 0","passed":1,"detail":"當期 ROA = 33.2%"},{"id":2,"category":"盈利能力","desc":"營業現金流 CFO > 0","passed":1,"detail":"自由現金流 = $445M"},{"id":3,"category":"盈利能力","desc":"資產回報率持續擴張 (ΔROA > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"回報率穩步領先同業基準"},{"id":4,"category":"盈利能力","desc":"應計利潤品質高 (CFO > 淨利潤)","passed":0,"detail":"真實現金流充沛，無虛報帳面獲利"},{"id":5,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"財務槓桿未惡化 (ΔLeverage ≤ 0)","passed":1,"detail":"總負債資產比率 = 25.4%"},{"id":6,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"短期流動性安全 (ΔLiquidity > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"流動比率 = 6.69"},{"id":7,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"股本未遭稀釋 (ΔShares ≤ 0)","passed":1,"detail":"未大幅增發新股割韭菜"},{"id":8,"category":"營運效率","desc":"毛利率擴張 (ΔMargin > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"產品定價權增強，毛利結構健康"},{"id":9,"category":"營運效率","desc":"資產週轉率提升 (ΔTurnover > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"每單位資產產出效益改善"}],"fair_val":139.77,"default_fair_val":139.77,"premium_pct":-29.9,"is_undervalued":true,"pe_trailing":4.8,"pe_forward":4.2,"pb_trailing":2.1,"pb_forward":1.9,"div_yield":12.45,"ps_ratio":2.8,"fcf_to_ev":8.44,"fcf_to_mcap":8.87,"liab_to_assets":25.4,"cash_to_assets":14.3,"current_ratio":6.69,"roe":44.5,"roa":33.2,"moat":{"ticker":"INSW","period":"2026Q3","m1_brand_pricing":{"score":3,"comment_zh":"海運業本質上是商品化行業，品牌和定價權的影響甚微。INSW 作為一家大型油輪營運商，其服務的客戶主要是大型石油公司和貿易商，這些客戶更關注運力、成本和可靠性，而非品牌聲譽。雖然公司可能在特定航線或長期合約中展現一定的議價能力，但整體而言，其定價能力受制於全球供需關係和宏觀經濟週期，缺乏顯著的品牌溢價或定價壁壘。與消費品或技術公司相比，其品牌價值對客戶決策的影響力微乎其微。","comment_en":"The shipping industry is inherently commoditized, with minimal impact from brand and pricing power. INSW, as a large tanker operator, primarily serves major oil companies and traders who prioritize capacity, cost, and reliability over brand reputation. While the company may exhibit some bargaining power on specific routes or in long-term contracts, its overall pricing power is constrained by global supply-demand dynamics and macroeconomic cycles, lacking significant brand premium or pricing barriers. Compared to consumer goods or technology companies, the influence of its brand value on customer decisions is negligible."},"m2_patents_regulatory":{"score":2,"comment_zh":"海運業的進入壁壘主要來自於船舶的資本密集度、營運的複雜性以及嚴格的國際海事法規。INSW 作為一家成熟的航運公司，擁有龐大的船隊和豐富的營運經驗，這構成了一定的進入門檻。然而，該行業並無專利或獨特的技術壁壘。法規遵循是營運的必要條件，但並非獨特的競爭優勢，因為所有參與者都必須遵守相同的國際規則。因此，在專利和特許權方面，INSW 的護城河非常薄弱。","comment_en":"Barriers to entry in the shipping industry primarily stem from the capital intensity of vessels, operational complexity, and stringent international maritime regulations. INSW, as an established shipping company, possesses a large fleet and extensive operational experience, which constitutes a certain entry threshold. However, the industry lacks patent or unique technological barriers. Regulatory compliance is a necessary condition for operation but not a unique competitive advantage, as all participants must adhere to the same international rules. Therefore, INSW's moat in terms of patents and regulatory exclusivity is very weak."},"m3_high_switching_costs":{"score":4,"comment_zh":"對於大型貨物運輸而言，客戶轉換供應商的成本相對較高，主要體現在尋找新船東、協商合約條款、以及確保運輸連續性和可靠性的時間與精力成本。INSW 的客戶，如大型石油公司，通常與其建立長期的合作關係，以確保穩定的運力供應。然而，這種關係更多是基於運力需求和成本效益，而非技術綁定或高度整合的系統。一旦合約結束，客戶仍有相對的選擇空間，轉換成本雖存在但並非難以逾越。","comment_en":"For large-scale cargo transportation, the cost for customers to switch suppliers is relatively high, mainly reflected in the time and effort required to find new shipowners, negotiate contract terms, and ensure transportation continuity and reliability. INSW's clients, such as major oil companies, typically establish long-term cooperative relationships to ensure stable capacity supply. However, this relationship is more based on capacity needs and cost-effectiveness rather than technological lock-in or highly integrated systems. Once a contract ends, customers still have considerable options, and while switching costs exist, they are not insurmountable."},"m4_network_effects":{"score":1,"comment_zh":"海運業，特別是油輪運輸，幾乎不存在網絡效應。網絡效應通常發生在平台型業務中，用戶越多，價值越大。在航運業，船東提供的是運輸服務，客戶需要的是將貨物從 A 點運到 B 點。INSW 的價值不隨客戶數量的增加而增加，反之亦然。雖然擁有龐大的船隊和廣泛的航線網絡可以提高營運效率和客戶服務能力，但這並非典型的網絡效應壁壘，不具備自我強化的增長機制。","comment_en":"The shipping industry, particularly oil tanker transportation, exhibits virtually no network effects. Network effects typically occur in platform-based businesses where more users lead to greater value. In the shipping industry, shipowners provide transportation services, and customers need to move goods from point A to point B. INSW's value does not increase with the number of customers, and vice versa. While a large fleet and extensive route network can enhance operational efficiency and customer service capabilities, this is not a typical network effect barrier and lacks a self-reinforcing growth mechanism."},"m5_cost_advantage_scale":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"INSW 作為全球領先的油輪公司之一，其規模帶來了顯著的成本優勢。大型船隊意味著在採購、維護、保險、融資以及船員管理等方面具有更強的議價能力和攤薄固定成本的能力。公司能夠承接更大規模的貨運訂單，並優化航線佈局以提高效率。這種規模經濟效應使得小型競爭對手難以在成本上與之匹敵，尤其是在市場低迷時期，規模較小的公司更容易面臨財務壓力。這是其核心競爭力之一。","comment_en":"As one of the world's leading tanker companies, INSW benefits from significant cost advantages due to its scale. A large fleet translates into stronger bargaining power in procurement, maintenance, insurance, financing, and crew management, as well as the ability to spread fixed costs. The company can undertake larger cargo orders and optimize route layouts for efficiency. This economy of scale makes it difficult for smaller competitors to match its cost structure, especially during market downturns when smaller companies are more susceptible to financial pressure. This is one of its core competitive strengths."},"m6_unique_geography_assets":{"score":2,"comment_zh":"海運業的資產主要是船舶，這些資產在地理上的獨特性非常有限。INSW 的船隊可以在全球範圍內運營，其價值在於船隊的總體規模和運營能力，而非特定地理位置的固定資產。雖然公司可能在某些關鍵航線上擁有較多的運力佈局，但這些航線本身並非獨特的地理資產，其他競爭者也可以進入。因此，在獨特的地理資產方面，INSW 的護城河幾乎不存在。","comment_en":"The primary assets in the shipping industry are vessels, which have very limited geographical uniqueness. INSW's fleet operates globally, and its value lies in the overall size and operational capability of the fleet, rather than fixed assets in specific geographic locations. While the company may have a significant capacity deployment on certain key routes, these routes themselves are not unique geographical assets, and other competitors can also access them. Therefore, INSW's moat regarding unique geographical assets is virtually non-existent."},"m7_operational_efficiency":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"INSW 在營運效率方面表現出色，這得益於其龐大的船隊管理經驗、先進的船舶技術以及對航線優化的持續投入。公司能夠有效管理燃料消耗、維護成本和船員調度，從而降低單位運輸成本。其高 ROE 和 ROA 表明了其卓越的盈利能力和資產運用效率。儘管海運業的整體效率受外部因素影響較大，但 INSW 透過精細化管理和技術升級，在行業內建立了相對領先的營運效率，這構成了一定的競爭壁壘。","comment_en":"INSW demonstrates strong operational efficiency, attributed to its extensive fleet management experience, advanced vessel technology, and continuous investment in route optimization. The company effectively manages fuel consumption, maintenance costs, and crew scheduling, thereby reducing per-unit transportation costs. Its high ROE and ROA indicate excellent profitability and asset utilization efficiency. Although overall industry efficiency is significantly influenced by external factors, INSW has established a relatively leading operational efficiency within the sector through meticulous management and technological upgrades, forming a certain competitive barrier."},"m8_capital_allocation":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"INSW 在資本配置方面展現了較高的水準，尤其是在當前市場環境下。公司透過股息支付、股票回購和償還債務等多種方式回饋股東，同時也積極進行船隊更新和擴張。其高 F-Score 和強勁的自由現金流表明了其財務健康和穩健的現金生成能力。管理層在平衡短期股東回報與長期資產投資方面做得較好，能夠在市場週期中靈活調整資本配置策略，為股東創造長期價值。","comment_en":"INSW demonstrates a high level of capital allocation, especially in the current market environment. The company returns value to shareholders through dividends, share buybacks, and debt repayment, while also actively pursuing fleet renewal and expansion. Its high F-Score and strong free cash flow indicate financial health and robust cash generation capabilities. Management strikes a good balance between short-term shareholder returns and long-term asset investments, flexibly adjusting capital allocation strategies through market cycles to create long-term value for shareholders."},"m9_customer_retention":{"score":5,"comment_zh":"INSW 的客戶留存率相對穩定，這主要得益於其可靠的服務、龐大的船隊規模以及與主要客戶建立的長期合作關係。大型石油公司和貿易商在選擇供應商時，會考慮運力穩定性、安全記錄和運營效率。INSW 在這些方面具有一定的優勢，能夠滿足客戶對可靠運輸的需求。然而，由於海運業的商品化屬性，客戶在合約到期後仍有較大的選擇空間，若有更具成本效益的替代方案，轉換的可能性依然存在。","comment_en":"INSW's customer retention rate is relatively stable, primarily due to its reliable service, large fleet size, and established long-term relationships with major clients. Large oil companies and traders consider capacity stability, safety records, and operational efficiency when selecting suppliers. INSW holds certain advantages in these areas, meeting customer demands for reliable transportation. However, due to the commoditized nature of the shipping industry, customers still have considerable options upon contract expiration, and the possibility of switching remains if more cost-effective alternatives emerge."},"m10_durability":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"海運業的週期性非常明顯，易受全球經濟、地緣政治和能源需求等宏觀因素影響，這限制了其長期穩定性。INSW 作為油輪營運商，其盈利能力會隨著市場供需的波動而劇烈變化。儘管公司透過規模、效率和資本配置來緩解週期性影響，並努力維持穩定的股息，但其業務的本質決定了其護城河的持久性相對有限。相較於具有持續定價權或網絡效應的行業，航運業的長期穩定性較弱。","comment_en":"The shipping industry is highly cyclical, susceptible to macroeconomic factors such as the global economy, geopolitics, and energy demand, which limits its long-term stability. As a tanker operator, INSW's profitability fluctuates significantly with market supply and demand dynamics. Although the company mitigates cyclical impacts through scale, efficiency, and capital allocation, and strives to maintain stable dividends, the inherent nature of its business dictates a relatively limited durability of its moat. Compared to industries with persistent pricing power or network effects, the long-term stability of the shipping sector is weaker."},"overall_moat_verdict_zh":"International Seaways (INSW) 在海運這個高度週期性且商品化的行業中運營。其核心競爭力體現在規模經濟帶來的成本優勢（M5）以及相對領先的營運效率（M7）和穩健的資本配置能力（M8）。然而，該行業缺乏品牌定價權（M1）、專利壁壘（M2）、網絡效應（M4）和獨特地理資產（M6），客戶轉換成本（M3）和客戶留存（M9）也相對有限。整體而言，INSW 的護城河屬於商品型，其競爭優勢主要依賴於卓越的執行力和成本控制，而非難以複製的特許經營權或網絡效應。其業務的持久性（M10）受行業週期性影響較大。","overall_moat_verdict_en":"International Seaways (INSW) operates in the highly cyclical and commoditized maritime shipping industry. Its core strengths lie in the cost advantages derived from economies of scale (M5), relatively leading operational efficiency (M7), and robust capital allocation capabilities (M8). However, the industry lacks brand pricing power (M1), patent barriers (M2), network effects (M4), and unique geographical assets (M6). Customer switching costs (M3) and retention (M9) are also relatively limited. Overall, INSW's moat is of a commodity type, with its competitive advantage primarily relying on excellent execution and cost control rather than hard-to-replicate franchises or network effects. The durability of its business (M10) is significantly influenced by industry cyclicality.","evidenceHash":"6a8fb90e8a4ffdd16b6dc2eb63cdb97929656f799bd45d24fa17dd9423158a39","assessmentPolicy":"buffett-moat-v3","model":"gemini-2.5-flash-lite","provider":"Vertex AI"},"ratingSources":{"moat":{"reason":null,"evidenceHash":"6a8fb90e8a4ffdd16b6dc2eb63cdb97929656f799bd45d24fa17dd9423158a39","currentEvidenceHash":"6a8fb90e8a4ffdd16b6dc2eb63cdb97929656f799bd45d24fa17dd9423158a39"},"fScore":{"score":8,"checkedAt":null},"zScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":"z","zone":"superRobust","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-08T01:39:54.036Z","evidenceHash":"917a46907b402d2097151338440de32ce9be0f4206f7c3a76422451473207793"},"mScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":null,"zone":"highRisk","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-08T01:39:54.036Z","evidenceHash":"917a46907b402d2097151338440de32ce9be0f4206f7c3a76422451473207793"}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/INSW.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/INSW.png","website":"https://intlseas.com","ceo":"Lois K. Zabrocky","full_time_employees":"2837","description":"International Seaways, Inc. (INSW) specializes in the global seaborne transport of crude oil and refined petroleum products, managing and operating a substantial fleet of ocean-going vessels. Its business is categorized into two key divisions: Crude Tankers and Product Carriers. By the close of 2021, the company managed an extensive fleet of 83 vessels, encompassing both owned and 12 chartered-in ships, alongside stakes in two floating storage and offloading (FSO) service vessels. Its diverse clientele spans independent and state-controlled oil enterprises, energy traders, refinery operators, and international governmental bodies. Originally incorporated in 1999 as OSG International, Inc., the firm adopted its current name, International Seaways, Inc., in October 2016. It maintains its corporate headquarters in New York, New York.","description_en":"International Seaways, Inc. (INSW) specializes in the global seaborne transport of crude oil and refined petroleum products, managing and operating a substantial fleet of ocean-going vessels. Its business is categorized into two key divisions: Crude Tankers and Product Carriers. By the close of 2021, the company managed an extensive fleet of 83 vessels, encompassing both owned and 12 chartered-in ships, alongside stakes in two floating storage and offloading (FSO) service vessels. Its diverse clientele spans independent and state-controlled oil enterprises, energy traders, refinery operators, and international governmental bodies. Originally incorporated in 1999 as OSG International, Inc., the firm adopted its current name, International Seaways, Inc., in October 2016. It maintains its corporate headquarters in New York, New York.","description_zh":"International Seaways, Inc.（美股代碼：INSW）為 Industrials 領域之重要企業，專注於 Marine Shipping 業務，具備清晰之商業壁壘與現金流創造能力。","address":"600 Third Avenue","city":"New York City","state":"NY","zip":"10016","country":"US","phone":"212 578 1600","full_address":"600 Third Avenue, New York City, NY 10016, US","range_52w":"46.09-126.274","year_high":126.274,"year_low":46.09,"all_time_high":0,"all_time_low":46.09,"inst_ownership_pct":null,"insider_ownership_pct":null,"top_holders":[],"insider_trades":[{"date":"2026-10-28","name":"Famatown Finance Ltd","title":"10 percent owner","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":100000,"price":121.55,"total_val":12.16},{"date":"2026-10-28","name":"Famatown Finance Ltd","title":"10 percent owner","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":37888,"price":121.99,"total_val":4.62},{"date":"2026-10-28","name":"Famatown Finance Ltd","title":"10 percent owner","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":1029,"price":124.48,"total_val":0.13},{"date":"2026-10-28","name":"Famatown Finance Ltd","title":"10 percent owner","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":64821,"price":125.05,"total_val":8.11},{"date":"2026-10-19","name":"Zabrocky Lois K","title":"director, officer: President & CEO","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":2000,"price":114.23,"total_val":0.23},{"date":"2026-10-16","name":"Famatown Finance Ltd","title":"10 percent owner","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":156924,"price":81.28,"total_val":12.75},{"date":"2026-10-16","name":"Famatown Finance Ltd","title":"10 percent owner","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":150000,"pri